						"type": "string",
						"value": "FACTORIAL\n\nThe Factorial calculates the factorial of the input and is often formulated as \"n!\" in mathematics.\nThe factorial function takes an in integer and multiplies it with all previous integers.\nFor example: 5! Would make 5*4*3*2*1 = 120 .\n\nDue to the astronomical results this function can create, the largest factorial Wire can calculate is 12!"
